\text{Area} = 0.78 \times \text{Area of the skin} = 0.78 \times \sqrt{\text{Weight in lb} \times \text{Height in in})}.
\]
**Step 1: Convert weight to pounds and height to inches**
Weight = 65 lb (given)
Height = 3 ft 6 in = 3 ft × 12 in/ft + 6 in = 36 in

**Step 2: Calculate the area of the skin**
\[
\text{Area} = 0.78 \times \sqrt{65 \times 36} = 0.78 \times \sqrt{2340} = 0.78 \times 46.9 \approx 36.502 \text{ m}^2.
\]
**Step 3: Convert the area to square meters**
1 in = 0.0254 m, so 36 in = 36 × 0.0254 m = 0.914 m.
\[
\text{Area} = 0.78 \times \sqrt{65 \times 36} = .78 \times \sqrt{2340} = 0.78 \times 46.9 = 36.502 \text{ m}^2.
\]
**Step 4: Calculate the dosage**
The dosage is given as 17.5 mg/m²/day. Multiply this by the area of the skin:
\[
\text{Delivery} = 17.5 \times 36.502 = 638.775 \text{ mg}.
\]
