","To determine the time required for the delivery of the loading dose, follow these steps:

1. **Convert the mass of the child from pounds to kilograms**:  
   \[
   \text{Weight in kg} = \frac{32 \text{ lb}}{2.205 \text{ lb/kg}} = 14.4 \text{ kg}
   \]

2. **Calculate the loading dose**:  
   \[
   \text{Loading load} = 20 \text{ mg/kg} \times 14.4 \text{ kg} = 288 \text{ mg}
   \]

3. **Calculate the time required**:  
   \[
   \text{Time} = \frac{288 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/min}} = 576 \text{ min}
   \]

