   \[ \text{Cu}(s) \rightarrow \text{Cu}^+ + e^-, \quad E^\circ^\circ_{\text{Cu}^+} = -0.342 \text{ V} \]

The standard cell potential \( E^\circ_{\text{cell}} \) is the difference between the standard reduction potential of the cathode and the standard reduction potential of the anode:

\[
E^\circ_{\text{cell}} = E^\circ_{\text{cathode}} - E^\circ_{\text{anode}} = 0.7996 \text{ V} - (-0..342 \text{ V}) = 1.1416 \text{ V}
\]

