The zeta potential (ζ) is the potential difference between the double layer and the surface of the particle. It is a measure of the degree of charge on the particle surface and affects the stability of the colloidal suspension. A higher zeta potential (either positive or negative) indicates a more stable suspension, as the particles are more likely to repel each other and not aggregate.

