1. **Calculate the normality of 6.00 M H\(_2\)SO\(_4\):**
   \[
   \text{N} = 2 \times \text{M}
   \]
   \[
   \text{N} = 2 \times 6.00 \text{ M} = 12.0 \text{ N}
   \]

2. **Calculate the moles of H\(_2\text{SO}_4\) in 10.0 liters of 2.00 N H\(_2\text{SO}_4\):**
   \[
   \text{Moles} = \text{Normality} \times \text{Volume (L)} \times \text{Molarity of H}_2\text{SO}_4
   \]
   \[
   \text{Moles} = 2.00 \text{ N} \times 10.0 \text{ L} = 20.0 \text{ moles}
   \]

3. **Calculate the moles of H\(_2\text{SO}_4\) in 20.0 liters of 3.00 M H\(_2\text{SO}_4\):**
   \[
   \text{Moles} = \text{Molarity} \times \text{Volume (L)}
   \]
