2. **Since \( A \triangleright B \subseteq A \)**:  
   This means any element in \( A \triangleright B \) must be in \( A \).  
   \[
   A \triangleright B = (A \setminus B) \cup (B \setminus A) \subseteq A.
   \]  
   This implies both \( A \setminus B \) and \( B \setminus A \) are in \( A \).  

