Given $f(x-1) > f(3-2x)$, since $f(x)$ is strictly increasing for $x \geq 0$, this implies $x-1 > 3-2x$.

Solving for $x$:
$x - 1 > 3 - 2x$
$3x > 4$
$x > \frac{4}{3}$

