   The inverse of the implication $A \cup B = A \implies A \cap B = B$ is:  
   \[
   A \cup B = A \implies A \not B \text{ (i.e., } A \cap B \neq B)
   \]

3. **Converse of the implication**:  
   The converse of the implication $A \cup B = A \implies A \cap B = B$ is:  
   \[
   A \cap B = B \implies A \cup B = A
   \]

