t' = 3 / sqrt(0.64)
t' = 3 / 0.8
t' = 3.75 years

Now, the question is about the clock in the cargo base. Since both clocks are on board the ship, they will experience the same time dilation effect. Therefore, the time measured by the clock in the cargo bay will be the same as the time measured by the clock in the cockpit, which is 3 years.

However, the question asks for the time shown on the clock in the cargo base when it is compared to a clock on Earth. This is the same as the time measured by the clock on the spaceship as measured by the Earth observer, which we calculated as 3.75 years.

