The uncertainty principle states:

\[
\Delta E \Delta t \geq \hbar
\]

For a short-lived particle, the lifetime \(\tau\) is related to the energy spread \(\Delta E\) as:

\[
\Delta E \approx \Gamma = \frac{\hbar}{\tau}
\]

Substituting \(\hbar = 1.054 \times 10^{-34} \, \text{J s}\) and \(\tau = 2.0 \times 10^{-23} \, \text{s}\):

\[
