\[
\dot{H}(t) = -w A e^{-w t} \cos(\omega t \pm \phi) - \omega A e^{-w t} \sin(\omega t \pm \phi)
\]

This can be rewritten as:

\[
\dot{H}(t) = A e^{-w t} \left(-w \cos(\omega t \pm \phi) - \omega \sin(\omega t \pm \phi)\right)
\]

Thus, the equation for \(\dot{H}(t)\) in terms of \(H(t)\) and \(w\) is:

\[
\dot{H}(t) = \frac{H(t)}{A e^{-w t}} \left(-w \cos(\omega t \pm \phi) - \omega \sin(\omega t \pm \phi)\right)
\]

